# Copy to .env (gitignored) and uncomment what you need. Every variable is optional.
# Assignments stay commented on purpose: for `make` targets a value set in .env wins over the same
# variable exported in your shell (`make VAR=value` wins over both).

# Where the source data comes from: synthetic (default, no credentials needed) or kaggle (the real
# Olist dataset; needs the token below and installs the `kaggle` extra on demand).
# DATA_SOURCE=kaggle

# Kaggle API token, only read when DATA_SOURCE=kaggle (Kaggle > Settings > API > Create New Token).
# Never commit a real value.
# KAGGLE_API_TOKEN=

# Root folder for source CSVs, landing Parquet, rejects, the ingest log and the DuckDB file.
# The Makefile defaults it to ./data as an absolute path.
# LAKEHOUSE_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/data

# DuckDB warehouse file that dbt writes. Default: $LAKEHOUSE_DATA_DIR/warehouse/lakehouse.duckdb
# LAKEHOUSE_DUCKDB_PATH=/absolute/path/to/lakehouse.duckdb

# Synthetic generator: number of orders (minimum 200) and RNG seed (same seed -> byte-identical
# CSVs).
# SYNTHETIC_ORDERS=5000
# SYNTHETIC_SEED=42

# Share of rejected rows above which a table load fails instead of landing (0.01 = 1%).
# MAX_REJECT_RATIO=0.01

# Airflow stack (`make up`): JWT secret and Fernet key. `make up` appends both to .env when they
# are missing, so you normally set nothing. By hand: openssl rand -hex 32  (JWT secret) and
# openssl rand -base64 32 | tr '+/' '-_'  (Fernet key). Never commit real values.
# AIRFLOW__API_AUTH__JWT_SECRET=
# AIRFLOW__CORE__FERNET_KEY=
